messages.content:
This repository is a static HTML/city-guide site, so the fastest realistic way to turn your concept into a playable game is a browser-based prototype, not a full Unity project. That gives you:
- rich visuals with HTML/CSS/Canvas
- a complete game loop and architecture
- GitHub Actions for deployment to Pages
- script language: JavaScript

Below is a complete starter implementation for a playable “Trust Protocol: Criminal Legends” prototype that matches your design brief and fits this repo’s HTML-first architecture.

Quick recommendation:
- Use a 2D top-down prototype first
- Keep the 3 heroes, trust meter, phone UI, and dungeon objective
- Deploy with GitHub Pages via GitHub Actions

Files to add:
- index.html
- style.css
- game.js
- .github/workflows/deploy.yml

Use these as your starter project files.

```html name=index.html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Trust Protocol: Criminal Legends</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css" />
</head>
<body>
  <div class="hud">
    <div class="brand">TRUST PROTOCOL</div>
    <div class="topbar">
      <div class="meter-wrap">
        <label>Trust</label>
        <div class="meter">
          <div id="trustFill"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="controls">1: Blackhujus &nbsp; 2: Mr. PING &nbsp; 3: Merhujus</div>
    </div>
    <div id="status">Mission: Reach the temple exit.</div>
  </div>

  <div id="phoneOverlay" class="phone hidden">
    <div class="phone-header">
      <span>Trust Protocol</span>
      <span id="phoneClose">✕</span>
    </div>
    <div class="phone-body">
      <h3>Criminal intel</h3>
      <p>Temple breach in progress. Team trust is critical.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Blackhujus: Brute force / tank</li>
        <li>Mr. PING: Speed / grappling / stealth</li>
        <li>Merhujus: Tech / bridge / support</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="map-mini">
        <div class="dot dot-a"></div>
        <div class="dot dot-b"></div>
        <div class="dot dot-c"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <canvas id="gameCanvas" width="960" height="600"></canvas>

  <script src="game.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

```css name=style.css
:root {
  --bg: #070b13;
  --panel: rgba(13, 20, 30, 0.8);
  --line: rgba(104, 134, 160, 0.5);
  --green: #59f7a4;
  --yellow: #f5d76e;
  --red: #ff5e62;
  --blue: #6bb9ff;
  --purple: #d39af7;
  --orange: #ffae57;
  --white: #ecf4ff;
  --shadow: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45);
}

* { box-sizing: border-box; }

body {
  margin: 0;
  background:
    radial-gradient(circle at top, rgba(81,95,120,0.22), transparent 35%),
    linear-gradient(180deg, #090d14, #04070b);
  color: var(--white);
  font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
  overflow: hidden;
}

#gameCanvas {
  display: block;
  margin: 0 auto;
  width: min(100vw, 960px);
  height: min(100vh - 90px, 600px);
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  background:
    linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(18, 31, 47, 0.9), rgba(11, 18, 28, 0.95)),
    #101822;
  box-shadow: 0 20px 60px var(--shadow);
  image-rendering: auto;
}

.hud {
  width: min(100vw, 960px);
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 10px 16px 0;
}

.brand {
  letter-spacing: 0.35rem;
  font-size: 0.8rem;
  color: var(--yellow);
  opacity: 0.9;
  margin-bottom: 6px;
}

.topbar {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 12px;
  background: var(--panel);
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  border-radius: 10px;
  padding: 10px 14px;
}

.meter-wrap {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 10px;
  min-width: 220px;
}

.meter-wrap label {
  font-size: 0.8rem;
  letter-spacing: 0.1rem;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--white);
  opacity: 0.9;
}

.meter {
  width: 140px;
  height: 12px;
  border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.15);
  background: rgba(255,255,255,0.05);
  border-radius: 999px;
  overflow: hidden;
}

#trustFill {
  width: 65%;
  height: 100%;
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--red), var(--yellow), var(--green));
  transition: width 0.2s ease;
}

.controls {
  font-size: 0.78rem;
  color: #d8e6ff;
  opacity: 0.85;
}

#status {
  background: var(--panel);
  border: 1px solid var(--line);
  margin-top: 8px;
  border-radius: 10px;
  padding: 10px 14px;
  font-size: 0.8rem;
  letter-spacing: 0.04rem;
  color: var(--white);
}

.phone {
  position: absolute;
  top: 100px;
  right: 25px;
  width: 300px;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(17, 24, 35, 0.95), rgba(10, 14, 20, 0.97));
  border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);
  border-radius: 20px;
  box-shadow: 0 14px 40px rgba(0,0,0,0.55);
  z-index: 10;
}

.phone.hidden {
  display: none;
}

.phone-header {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
  padding: 10px 14px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--green);
}

#phoneClose {
  cursor: pointer;
}

.phone-body {
  padding: 14px;
  font-size: 0.9rem;
  line-height: 1.5;
}

.phone-body ul {
  padding-left: 18px;
  margin: 10px 0;
}

.map-mini {
  position: relative;
  height: 110px;
  margin-top: 12px;
  border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.12);
  background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03);
  border-radius: 10px;
  overflow: hidden;
}

.dot {
  position: absolute;
  width: 12px;
  height: 12px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: var(--blue);
  box-shadow: 0 0 18px var(--blue);
}

.dot-a { left: 16%; top: 24%; background: var(--green); }
.dot-b { left: 48%; top: 62%; background: var(--orange); }
.dot-c { left: 70%; top: 38%; background: var(--purple); }

@media (max-width: 640px) {
  .topbar {
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }
  .controls {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
  }
  .phone {
    right: 12px;
    width: 260px;
  }
}
```

```javascript name=game.js
const canvas = document.getElementById("gameCanvas");
const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");

const statusEl = document.getElementById("status");
const trustFill = document.getElementById("trustFill");
const phoneOverlay = document.getElementById("phoneOverlay");
const phoneClose = document.getElementById("phoneClose");

const keys = {};
const heroNames = ["Blackhujus", "Mr. PING", "Merhujus"];
const heroColors = ["#ff7d5c", "#7ae7ff", "#a5ff9c"];

const world = {
  width: canvas.width,
  height: canvas.height,
  walls: [
    { x: 120, y: 110, w: 300, h: 18 },
    { x: 280, y: 200, w: 18, h: 220 },
    { x: 520, y: 150, w: 18, h: 260 },
    { x: 170, y: 420, w: 360, h: 18 },
    { x: 680, y: 110, w: 18, h: 330 },
  ],
  switches: [
    { x: 230, y: 80, id: "A", active: false },
    { x: 620, y: 420, id: "B", active: false },
    { x: 820, y: 180, id: "C", active: false },
  ],
  exit: { x: 860, y: 500, w: 50, h: 50 },
  loot: [
    { x: 200, y: 300, picked: false },
    { x: 760, y: 250, picked: false },
    { x: 610, y: 120, picked: false }
  ],
  truck: { x: 800, y: 320, w: 90, h: 40 }
};

let trust = 65;
let selectedHero = 0;
let gameWon = false;

const heroData = [
  { name: "Blackhujus", x: 80, y: 180, r: 14, color: heroColors[0], speed: 2.2, role: "Tank" },
  { name: "Mr. PING", x: 80, y: 250, r: 12, color: heroColors[1], speed: 2.7, role: "Rogue" },
  { name: "Merhujus", x: 80, y: 320, r: 13, color: heroColors[2], speed: 2.4, role: "Engineer" }
];

function clamp(value, min, max) {
  return Math.min(Math.max(value, min), max);
}

function setStatus(message) {
  statusEl.textContent = "Mission: " + message;
}

function updateTrustBar() {
  trustFill.style.width = trust + "%";
}

function togglePhone() {
  phoneOverlay.classList.toggle("hidden");
}

function rectsIntersect(a, b) {
  return a.x < b.x + b.w &&
         a.x + a.w > b.x &&
         a.y < b.y + b.h &&
         a.y + a.h > b.y;
}

function circleRectCollision(circle, rect) {
  const closestX = clamp(circle.x, rect.x, rect.x + rect.w);
  const closestY = clamp(circle.y, rect.y, rect.y + rect.h);
  const dx = circle.x - closestX;
  const dy = circle.y - closestY;
  return (dx * dx + dy * dy) < circle.r * circle.r;
}

function moveHero(hero, dx, dy) {
  const nextX = hero.x + dx;
  const nextY = hero.y + dy;

  const test = { x: nextX - hero.r, y: nextY - hero.r, w: hero.r * 2, h: hero.r * 2 };

  let canMove = true;
  for (const wall of world.walls) {
    if (rectsIntersect(test, wall)) {
      canMove = false;
      break;
    }
  }

  if (canMove) {
    hero.x = clamp(nextX, 20, canvas.width - 20);
    hero.y = clamp(nextY, 20, canvas.height - 20);
  } else {
    trust = clamp(trust - 1, 0, 100);
    updateTrustBar();
  }
}

function interact() {
  const hero = heroData[selectedHero];
  const interactRadius = 26;

  for (const s of world.switches) {
    if (Math.hypot(hero.x - s.x, hero.y - s.y) < interactRadius) {
      s.active = true;
      setStatus("Switch activated: " + s.id);
      return;
    }
  }

  const truckZone = {
    x: world.truck.x - 18,
    y: world.truck.y - 18,
    w: world.truck.w + 36,
    h: world.truck.h + 36
  };

  if (rectsIntersect(
    { x: hero.x - hero.r, y: hero.y - hero.r, w: hero.r*2, h: hero.r*2 },
    truckZone
  )) {
    setStatus("Merhujus' truck is ready. Team movement is synced.");
    return;
  }

  for (const loot of world.loot) {
    if (!loot.picked && Math.hypot(hero.x - loot.x, hero.y - loot.y) < 20) {
      loot.picked = true;
      trust = clamp(trust - 8, 0, 100);
      setStatus(hero.name + " took the loot selfishly. Trust dropped.");
      updateTrustBar();
      return;
    }
  }

  const exitRect = world.exit;
  if (circleRectCollision({ x: hero.x, y: hero.y, r: hero.r }, exitRect)) {
    const allSwitches = world.switches.every(s => s.active);

    if (allSwitches) {
      gameWon = true;
      setStatus("Temple unlocked. Criminal empire secured.");
    } else {
      setStatus("Need all three temple switches to unlock the exit.");
    }
  }
}

document.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => {
  keys[e.key.toLowerCase()] = true;

  if (e.key === "1") selectedHero = 0;
  if (e.key === "2") selectedHero = 1;
  if (e.key === "3") selectedHero = 2;

  if (e.key.toLowerCase() === "e") {
    interact();
  }

  if (e.key.toLowerCase() === "t") {
    togglePhone();
  }

  if (e.key.toLowerCase() === " ") {
    if (!gameWon) {
      trust = clamp(trust + 5, 0, 100);
      setStatus("Team sync boost: trust increased.");
      updateTrustBar();
    }
  }
});

document.addEventListener("keyup", (e) => {
  keys[e.key.toLowerCase()] = false;
});

phoneClose.addEventListener("click", togglePhone);

function update() {
  if (gameWon) return;

  const hero = heroData[selectedHero];
  let dx = 0;
  let dy = 0;

  if (keys["w"] || keys["arrowup"]) dy -= hero.speed;
  if (keys["s"] || keys["arrowdown"]) dy += hero.speed;
  if (keys["a"] || keys["arrowleft"]) dx -= hero.speed;
  if (keys["d"] || keys["arrowright"]) dx += hero.speed;

  if (dx !== 0 || dy !== 0) {
    moveHero(hero, dx, dy);
  }

  // If the selected hero is on the truck, allow team movement boost
  const truckZone = { x: world.truck.x, y: world.truck.y, w: world.truck.w, h: world.truck.h };
  if (circleRectCollision({ x: hero.x, y: hero.y, r: hero.r }, truckZone)) {
    trust = clamp(trust + 0.12, 0, 100);
    updateTrustBar();
  }

  if (world.switches.every(s => s.active)) {
    setStatus("All temple switches are active. Escape is open!");
  } else {
    const active = world.switches.filter(s => s.active).length;
    setStatus("Temple locks: " + active + "/3 active");
  }

  // Simple co-op trust reward if all heroes are close
  const closeEnough = heroData.every((h) => Math.hypot(h.x - hero.x, h.y - hero.y) < 120);
  if (closeEnough && trust < 100) {
    trust = clamp(trust + 0.04, 0, 100);
    updateTrustBar();
  }
}

function drawSwitch(s) {
  ctx.fillStyle = s.active ? "#5ef7a3" : "#ff7b7b";
  ctx.beginPath();
  ctx.arc(s.x, s.y, 10, 0, Math.PI * 2);
  ctx.fill();

  ctx.strokeStyle = "rgba(255,255,255,0.5)";
  ctx.beginPath();
  ctx.arc(s.x, s.y, 16, 0, Math.PI * 2);
  ctx.stroke();
}

function drawTruck() {
  const { x, y, w, h } = world.truck;
  ctx.fillStyle = "#d1b67d";
  ctx.fillRect(x, y, w, h);
  ctx.fillStyle = "#4a3f2f";
  ctx.fillRect(x + 18, y + 8, 20, 12);
  ctx.fillRect(x + 50, y + 8, 20, 12);
  ctx.fillStyle = "#2f2b2a";
  ctx.fillRect(x + 28, y + 26, 28, 8);
}

function drawLoot() {
  for (const loot of world.loot) {
    if (loot.picked) continue;
    ctx.fillStyle = "#f6d365";
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(loot.x, loot.y, 8, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.fill();
  }
}

function drawExit() {
  const { x, y, w, h } = world.exit;
  ctx.strokeStyle = "#7ae7ff";
  ctx.lineWidth = 3;
  ctx.strokeRect(x, y, w, h);
}

function drawWalls() {
  ctx.fillStyle = "#2d3e53";
  for (const wall of world.walls) {
    ctx.fillRect(wall.x, wall.y, wall.w, wall.h);
  }
}

function drawHeroes() {
  heroData.forEach((hero, index) => {
    ctx.fillStyle = hero.color;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(hero.x, hero.y, hero.r, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.fill();

    if (index === selectedHero) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = "#fff4ad";
      ctx.lineWidth = 3;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(hero.x, hero.y, hero.r + 6, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.stroke();
    }

    ctx.fillStyle = "#ecf4ff";
    ctx.font = "12px Arial";
    ctx.fillText(hero.name.split(" ")[0], hero.x - 18, hero.y - 18);
  });
}

function draw() {
  ctx.clearRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);

  // floor
  ctx.fillStyle = "#0e1721";
  ctx.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);

  // subtle grid
  ctx.strokeStyle = "rgba(255,255,255,0.04)";
  ctx.lineWidth = 1;
  for (let x = 0; x <= canvas.width; x += 40) {
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x, 0);
    ctx.lineTo(x, canvas.height);
    ctx.stroke();
  }
  for (let y = 0; y <= canvas.height; y += 40) {
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(0, y);
    ctx.lineTo(canvas.width, y);
    ctx.stroke();
  }

  drawWalls();
  drawTruck();
  drawSwitches();
  drawLoot();
  drawExit();
  drawHeroes();

  if (gameWon) {
    ctx.fillStyle = "rgba(0,0,0,0.45)";
    ctx.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);
    ctx.fillStyle = "#f4f9ff";
    ctx.font = "bold 38px Arial";
    ctx.fillText("TEMPLE SECURED", 280, 290);
    ctx.font = "20px Arial";
    ctx.fillText("The trust protocol holds. Mission complete.", 250, 330);
  }
}

function drawSwitches() {
  for (const s of world.switches) {
    drawSwitch(s);
  }
}

function loop() {
  update();
  draw();
  requestAnimationFrame(loop);
}

updateTrustBar();
setStatus("Reach the temple exit and activate all switches.");
requestAnimationFrame(loop);
```

```yaml name=.github/workflows/deploy.yml
name: Deploy Trust Protocol Game

on:
  push:
    branches: [ main ]
  workflow_dispatch:

permissions:
  contents: read
  pages: write
  id-token: write

jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - name: Checkout
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Setup Pages
        uses: actions/configure-pages@v5

      - name: Upload static site
        uses: actions/upload-pages-artifact@v3
        with:
          path: .

  deploy:
    environment:
      name: github-pages
      url: ${{ steps.deployment.outputs.page_url }}
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    needs: build
    steps:
      - name: Deploy to GitHub Pages
        id: deployment
        uses: actions/deploy-pages@v4
```

Recommended architecture for future expansion:
- Game systems:
  - PlayerController
  - TrustMeter
  - SmartphoneUI
  - DungeonObjective
  - Interactables
  - Co-opSync
- Suggested next layers:
  - 3 playable heroes with unique stats
  - truck physics
  - more dungeon rooms
  - networked co-op layer for real multiplayer
  - art style: neon criminal, cinematic lighting, stylized UI
- Best script stack:
  - JavaScript for browser prototype
  - TypeScript for production-scale expansion
  - Optional Phaser or Three.js for richer visuals

If you want, I can continue with one of these next:
- build a richer 3D/2.5D version using Phaser
- create a full “safe house” and dungeon room flow
- generate a full GitHub Pages-ready project structure for this repo
- write the art/game design document in code-ready form for the next milestone

I prepared the full GitHub Pages-ready project plan and code, but I could not push it into dawidmillenium-design/coworking because the GitHub write permission for that repo is not available from this session.

The correct repo-compatible structure is:

- docs/
  - index.html
  - style.css
  - game.js
  - assets/
    - logo.svg
- .github/workflows/
  - deploy-pages.yml
- design/
  - ART_GDD.md
- README.md

This fits the repo’s current static-site style and lets GitHub Pages serve the game from docs/.

